Package: umwand
Version: 0.1.1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Depends: libglib2.0-bin, xdg-utils
Recommends: libreoffice-writer, libreoffice-calc, libreoffice-impress
Suggests: this2that
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/excelano/umwand
Description: Open Office Open XML files as OpenDocument
 umwand registers as the handler for .docx, .xlsx and .pptx files. Opening
 one converts it to .odt, .ods or .odp and opens the result in the default
 application for OpenDocument. The converted file sits beside the original,
 which is never changed; a file opened from a temporary or read-only
 location is converted into an umwand folder under Documents instead.
 Opening the same file again reuses a conversion that is newer than it.
 .
 LibreOffice does the conversion when it is installed. Without it, the
 this2that converters handle Word and Excel files, and presentations open
 unconverted. Digitally signed files, which conversion would invalidate,
 and files no converter manages are passed to the next application
 registered for their type.
